3.—(1) A person is exempt from section 33(2) of the Act for acquiring, or taking part in the acquisition of, any non‑arms weapon from a supplier who is, at the time of the supply, exempt under paragraph 2(4) from section 32 of the Act.
(2) In this paragraph, “non‑arms weapon” means any weapon that is not any of the following:
(a)a bayonet, sword or dagger;
(b)a spear or spearhead;
(c)an arrow with any of the following points:
(i)a broadhead tip;
(ii)a field arrow tip;
(iii)a blunt arrow tip;
(iv)a grabbing arrow tip;
(v)a fishing arrow tip;
(d)an arbalest;
(e)a device (commonly called a crossbow) consisting of a bow fitted transversely on a stock that has a groove or barrel, designed to direct an arrow or a bolt;
(f)a bow with a draw weight of more than 27.215 kilograms.
